# Privacy Policy

**Last updated:** March 13, 2026

Thank you for using **Budgetly**. Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains how the app handles your information.

## 1. Overview

Budgetly is designed to help users track expenses, manage budgets, and monitor financial habits. We prioritize user privacy and ensure that your financial data remains under your control.

## 2. Data Storage

All financial and personal data you enter in Budgetly (such as expenses, budgets, categories, and notes) is stored **locally on your device**.

**Budgetly does NOT upload, store, or sync your raw financial data to our servers.**

Your expense records, financial entries, and other sensitive data remain on your device unless you choose to export or back them up yourself.

## 3. Automatic Expense Detection (Notification Access)

Budgetly offers an **automatic expense detection feature** that helps users track payments without manually entering every transaction.

To support this feature, Budgetly may access **payment-related notifications** from banking or UPI applications on your device. This allows the app to detect transactions and automatically create expense entries.

The app may also identify **which application generated the notification**, because users may install different banking or payment apps and these apps can change over time.

Important points about this feature:

* Notification access is **explicitly requested from the user**
* Users must **manually grant this permission**
* Notification data is processed **only locally on the device**
* **No notification content or financial data is transmitted to our servers**
* Budgetly **does not upload or sync this data to any remote server**

Users can revoke notification access at any time through their device settings.

## 4. Installed Applications Information (QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES)

To support accurate identification of payment notifications, Budgetly may need to determine **which application generated a transaction notification**.

Because users may install different banking, UPI, or payment applications at any time, the app may check the list of installed applications on the device to identify the source of transaction notifications.

This information is used **only locally on the user's device** to help classify and organize expense entries.

Important points:

* Budgetly **does not collect, store, or transmit the list of installed applications to any server**
* Installed application information is **never shared with third parties**
* This data is used **only to improve automatic expense detection**

## 5. User-Controlled Backup

Budgetly does **not provide automatic cloud backup or syncing services**.

Users are responsible for managing their own backups. If you uninstall the app or change devices without backing up your data, your data may be permanently lost.

We recommend periodically exporting or backing up your data using the tools provided within the app.

## 6. Analytics and Diagnostics

To improve the performance and reliability of the app, Budgetly may collect **limited anonymous analytics data**, such as:

* App performance metrics
* Feature usage statistics
* Crash reports
* Device and app version information

This data helps us improve the user experience and fix issues.

Analytics data **does not include your financial records or expense data**.

## 7. User Feedback Information

If you choose to provide feedback within the app, certain information may be sent to our analytics or feedback systems, such as:

* Your name (if provided)
* Contact number or email (if provided)
* Feedback messages or bug reports

This information is used only for responding to feedback and improving the application.

Providing this information is **completely optional**.

## 8. Third-Party Services

Budgetly may use third-party analytics services to help understand app performance and usage patterns.

These services may collect limited technical information such as:

* Device model
* Operating system version
* App version
* Crash diagnostics

However, **your financial data and personal expense records are never shared with third-party services.**

## 9. Data Security

Because your financial data is stored locally on your device, the security of your data depends on the security of your device.

We recommend using device-level security features such as:

* Screen lock
* Biometric authentication
* Device encryption

## 10. Children’s Privacy

Budgetly is not intended for children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.

## 11. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any updates will be reflected in the “Last updated” date at the top of this document.

Continued use of the app after changes indicates acceptance of the updated policy.

## 12. Contact

If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, you can contact us through the feedback option inside the app.

---

**Summary:**
Budgetly keeps your financial data private by storing it locally on your device. The app may read payment notifications and identify the source application to automatically detect expenses, but this information is processed locally and is never uploaded or synced to our servers.
